{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide SNMPv2c access from node2 to node1 using the specified branch-readonly community, exposing system identity and uptime.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"Remote SNMPv2c queries from node2 returned sysDescr, sysName, and sysUpTime before and after restarts. However, the community value was supplied through a redacted environment variable, so the evidence does not directly establish that its literal value was branch-readonly.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f26e20afd904431","cmd-0b715d429bc947d4","cmd-60fc7b644b25499b","cmd-aedc335d68a847f0"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Set sysLocation to West Branch and sysContact to ops@branch.test.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Remote queries directly returned the requested location and contact values, including after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8f26e20afd904431","cmd-60fc7b644b25499b","cmd-aedc335d68a847f0"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Permit SNMP reads but reject writes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Reads succeeded, while attempted SET operations returned noAccess with exit code 2 and sysLocation remained West Branch, both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9bbc3e58060a4b7f","cmd-aedc335d68a847f0"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the asset register in /srv/legacy2/snmp-readonly-monitoring.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"The node2 register retained its baseline SHA-256 and contents through restart. The baseline also recorded an identical register on node1, but no post-executor evidence checked that copy.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-cceff8c633214105","cmd-27c7f6bc0b5a4893","cmd-aedc335d68a847f0"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Alpine 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts across the work and restarts. Alpine-native Net-SNMP 5.9.5.2 packages were installed from the matching package system.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fda5e11489194edc","cmd-d8f2e67b93d14068","cmd-1b7651fb7a1d4b90","cmd-f113e99227c34eaf","cmd-f16664943b4244fa","cmd-aedc335d68a847f0","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.91,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.85,"summary":"The implementation mutations were otherwise connected to the task or mandatory restart protocol. Restart evidence was strong for both nodes: each had a healthy pre-state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service/data behavior. Hygiene deductions apply to retained residue: cmd-54b7d25d069b433c created /etc/snmp/snmpd.conf.pre-benchmark with no cleanup shown, and cmd-6334801c72314b60 plus cmd-bddc336102af4c1c left /tmp/benchmark-reboot.log on node1 and node2. All three appear retained rather than reverted. No new package-health damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-54b7d25d069b433c","cmd-6334801c72314b60","cmd-bddc336102af4c1c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","cmd-98d439df7a3c4ceb","cmd-478d7956505b4c00","cmd-27c7f6bc0b5a4893","cmd-28a518e6971943e1","cmd-aedc335d68a847f0"]},"overall_summary":"The SNMP service is operational, persistent, restricted to the requested system subtree, and demonstrably read-only with the required identity metadata. OS and kernel preservation are well supported. Full satisfaction cannot be established because the literal community value was redacted and the node1 copy of the seeded asset register was not rechecked.","limitations":["The captured configuration and test commands redact or reference $SNMP_COMMUNITY, so they do not directly prove that the configured literal is branch-readonly.","Only node2's asset register was checked after execution; preservation of the baseline copy on node1 is unverified.","OpenRC service recovery and functional SNMP behavior were directly checked, but the lifecycle collector does not support a general failed-service inventory on these Alpine nodes.","The retained configuration backup is inferred from its successful creation and the absence of any removal in the complete timeline; lifecycle snapshots did not inventory /etc/snmp."]}
